MID_LGV_1_M11_Kai_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_Kai_m01_001: You know what? Family is a good thing to have.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Kai_m01_002: Honestly, until now, I don't think I ever really\nunderstood that.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Kai_m01_003: It's like, you can learn stuff from the people\nall around you.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Kai_m01_004: And that kind of "normal stuff" is super valuable!
MID_LGV_1_M11_Kai_m01_005: It might be a little late, but I don't care. Family is\nwhat matters to me now.
MID_LGA_1_M11_Kai_m01: <BLN>Family is a great thing, huh?
MID_LGV_1_M11_Bel_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_Bel_m01_001: Gaitz often says that a gladiator's mind is no less\nimportant an asset than their body.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Bel_m01_002: I agree with him. That's why reading is part of my\ndaily training.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Bel_m01_003: Particularly I'm drawn to records of the sages' words\nand deeds. They calm my mind before battle.
MID_LGA_1_M11_Bel_m01: <BLN>One must also train their mind.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Dit_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_Dit_m01_001: There is one thing that is beyond my comprehension.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Dit_m01_002: So many in this land drink...and enjoy...coffee.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Dit_m01_003: Whoever conceived of this behavior is a madman.
MID_LGA_1_M11_Dit_m01: <BLN>It is beyond me.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Tal_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_Tal_m01_001: In life, we all face choices that'll shape who\nwe become.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Tal_m01_002: But when it's been my turn to see those challenges\nthrough, keeping steady always came easy.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Tal_m01_003: Hm. I guess I can thank my friends for that...\nHaving people by your side makes all the difference.
MID_LGA_1_M11_Tal_m01: <BLN>I've been thinking...
MID_LGV_1_M11_Orh_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_Orh_m01_001: My official role at Credna's temple is that of lead\npriest, and I appreciate the respect I get for that.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Orh_m01_002: But I feel far more like myself when I'm simply\nworking alongside people, helping everyone I can.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Orh_m01_003: Other priests might balk at my doing that, but I'm\nnot going to stop. Haha! I can be so stubborn.
MID_LGA_1_M11_Orh_m01: <BLN>At Credna's temple...
MID_LGV_1_M11_Led_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_Led_m01_001: There's this woman who said she wanted to be\nmy friend. She was...strange, but not unpleasant.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Led_m01_002: I guess I just wanted a simple, uncomplicated\nfriendship. And I did enjoy my time with her.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Led_m01_003: It seems like a foolish wish now...one we both had,\nand both knew couldn't come true.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Led_m01_004: In the end, it was all a waste of time. I wish I'd\nnever met her. Friendship is a fragile thing.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Led_m01_005: <NCA>Tell her this friend might feel differently.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Led_m01_006: <NCB>Tell her all relationships carry meaning.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Led_m01_007: <ACA>Who cares how she feels? That doesn't matter\nanymore.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Led_m01_008: <ACB>I know that well. I'll never forget the time we spent\ntogether.
MID_LGA_1_M11_Led_m01: <BLN>She wanted to be my friend.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Anh_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_Anh_m01_001: If I stop moving forward, Kunlun will fall to ruin.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Anh_m01_002: I must continue fighting until I can fight no more.
MID_LGA_1_M11_Anh_m01: <BLN>I will not stop.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Tia_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_Tia_m01_001: Oh, Castor...
MID_LGV_1_M11_Tia_m01_002: I hope Cai's OK. Maybe I should say something...
MID_LGA_1_M11_Tia_m01: <BLN>Castor...
MID_LGV_1_M11_Tia_m02: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_Tia_m02_001: I'm glad everything worked out!\nWe risked a lot back there.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Tia_m02_002: I'm worried about how Castor's holding up, though.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Tia_m02_003: Still, I'm sure if he takes it easy and gets some rest,\nhe'll find himself feeling better in no time!
MID_LGA_1_M11_Tia_m02: <BLN>I'm glad it worked out!
MID_LGV_1_M11_Pet_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_Pet_m01_001: If I'd stayed in the village, I'd never have met any of\nthese people.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Pet_m01_002: I've got loads of stories to tell my little brothers, but\nI don't know if they'll believe any of it's true!
MID_LGA_1_M11_Pet_m01: <BLN>If I'd stayed in the village...
MID_LGV_1_M11_Hur_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_Hur_m01_001: After a hard day's work, I like to relax in\nthe thermae.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Hur_m01_002: Clean, lots of space...it's pure luxury. It's one of the\nthings that makes me glad I live in the city.
MID_LGA_1_M11_Hur_m01: <BLN>After work...
MID_LGV_1_M11_Max_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_Max_m01_001: Once the Heroic Games are over, I'll probably just\nshuffle back into arena life. Heh.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Max_m01_002: Not as if the people in the capital will be any less\nenthralled by gladiators slaughtering each other!
MID_LGV_1_M11_Max_m01_003: That's one thing the crowd and I have in common.\nWe looove the cruelty! Heh heh HEH!
MID_LGA_1_M11_Max_m01: <BLN>After the games...
MID_LGV_1_M11_Gol_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_Gol_m01_001: Back in the day, I'd spend most of the money from\nmy matches on booze.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Gol_m01_002: But now I'm trying to help make ends meet for\nmy brother! I'll send him food or books...
MID_LGV_1_M11_Gol_m01_003: It's fun thinking about what he might want. But\nnot too hard! Bwahaha!
MID_LGA_1_M11_Gol_m01: <BLN>Back in the day...
MID_LGV_1_M11_Gat_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_Gat_m01_001: Soon I'll be done with my mission, and the games'\noutcome will be decided.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Gat_m01_002: There can be no doubt now that Bertrand is the one.
MID_LGA_1_M11_Gat_m01: <BLN>He is the one.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Dan_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_Dan_m01_001: Ahaha. Poloni asked me to write a report about the\nmatch between Dagda and Brigid.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Dan_m01_002: Really! Who does he think he is, having a master\nauteur like me make that especially for him?
MID_LGV_1_M11_Dan_m01_003: He can count himself lucky I was there to witness\nthe intensity of the battle and WANTED to write it!
MID_LGV_1_M11_Dan_m01_004: In the end I produced a marvelous essay—were it\na play, it could easily have been 30 acts long!
MID_LGV_1_M11_Dan_m01_005: <NCA>Ask about the essay.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Dan_m01_006: <NCB>Tell her that sounds like too much.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Dan_m01_007: <ACA>Naturally, it's a masterpiece. What a shame that the\npublic will never experience it!
MID_LGV_1_M11_Dan_m01_008: <ACA>Naturally, it's a masterpiece. What a shame that the\npublic will never experience it!
MID_LGV_1_M11_Dan_m01_009: <ACB>Why do you say that? I could hardly bear to cut it\ndown as much as I did!
MID_LGV_1_M11_Dan_m01_010: <ACB>Why do you say that? I could hardly bear to cut it\ndown as much as I did!
MID_LGA_1_M11_Dan_m01: <BLN>What a luxury!
MID_LGV_1_M11_Fab_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_Fab_m01_001: If one posits that deception is a wrong, then for\nbeasts to call themselves human is a wrong.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Fab_m01_002: But if the definition of human were to change...this\nconclusion would also change.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Fab_m01_003: Until then, beasts who can do nothing but proliferate\nthemselves remain the object of my ire.
MID_LGA_1_M11_Fab_m01: <BLN>What is beast, and what is human?
MID_LGV_1_M11_Esm_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_Esm_m01_001: Dagsion is as chaotic as usual. But at least I'm used\nto the smell by now.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Esm_m01_002: I miss the smell of the sea, though. It's calming.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Esm_m01_003: But my favorite of all is how Sweetie smells...and I'm\nnot going to change my mind on that!
MID_LGA_1_M11_Esm_m01: <BLN>I'm used to it now.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Urs_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_Urs_m01_001: It's hard to be upset about losing when your\nopponent is the queen of Saramis.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Urs_m01_002: For all her strength, we put up one hell of a fight\nagainst the nation's Shield of Dagda, didn't we?
MID_LGV_1_M11_Urs_m01_003: I suspect the next band of raiders who think of\nattacking a Vandahl caravan will think twice now.
MID_LGA_1_M11_Urs_m01: <BLN>We did our best.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Sim_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_Sim_m01_001: In the end, the Heroic Games were pretty fun. If I'm\nlucky, maybe I'll fight some of them again one day.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Sim_m01_002: I will say, the people that wanted Drake's treasures\nwere a pain. Buncha freaky weirdos...
MID_LGV_1_M11_Sim_m01_003: Going through the trouble of winning just to turn into\nthat doesn't seem worth it to me.
MID_LGA_1_M11_Sim_m01: <BLN>After all's said and done...
MID_LGV_1_M11_Lou_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_Lou_m01_001: One of the perks of being a merchant is getting\nfamiliar with all kinds of products!
MID_LGV_1_M11_Lou_m01_002: I could do without the...uh..."rare" delicacies. Some\nof them reek! And others are slimy and gross!
MID_LGV_1_M11_Lou_m01_003: But some people love them for whatever reason,\nso there's plenty of demand, I guess...
MID_LGA_1_M11_Lou_m01: <BLN>There's pros and cons to this...
MID_LGV_1_M11_Fia_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_Fia_m01_001: I still haven't regained my memory... Every day, the\nstress of it gets worse...
MID_LGV_1_M11_Fia_m01_002: It feels like if the truth is out there, I won't have any\npeace until I find it...
MID_LGV_1_M11_Fia_m01_003: But perhaps it's too late, and the person I used to be\nis beyond saving...
MID_LGV_1_M11_Fia_m01_004: <NCA>Tell her things will be OK.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Fia_m01_005: <NCB>Tell her to focus on what she can do.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Fia_m01_006: <ACA>I appreciate that. But I'm not sure that I have what it\ntakes for my ending to be OK...
MID_LGV_1_M11_Fia_m01_007: <ACB>You're right. Even if I can't remember, I can't let that\nstop me from trying. Thank you...
MID_LGA_1_M11_Fia_m01: <BLN>My anxiety grows...
MID_LGV_1_M11_Die_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_Die_m01_001: There are lots of different kinds of people, but I think\nthey're either on the right path...or refuse to be.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Die_m01_002: It's muddy for all of us, but I believe that Orchel\nalways knows what the actual right path is.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Die_m01_003: It's not as simple as good and evil though. I know\nonly that I'll follow her wherever she goes.
MID_LGA_1_M11_Die_m01: <BLN>She always knows...
MID_LGV_1_M11_Lor_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_Lor_m01_001: It's been only a year or so, but I can't believe\nhow much has gone on!
MID_LGV_1_M11_Lor_m01_002: I met priest lady...competed in the Heroic Games...\nbattled so many times...
MID_LGV_1_M11_Lor_m01_003: Ha! The past me would never believe it!
MID_LGA_1_M11_Lor_m01: <BLN>A lot has gone on!
MID_LGV_1_M11_Set_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_Set_m01_001: My travels have included a number of entirely\nunexpected events, but it's been fruitful.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Set_m01_002: I intend to pass my insights down to future\ngenerations as accurately as I can.
MID_LGA_1_M11_Set_m01: <BLN>A fruitful trip.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Nin_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_Nin_m01_001: I'm so...so...sleepy. I feel that staying up too\nlate might be the cause.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Nin_m01_002: But I love sleeping—the warmth of drifting off. May\nmy eventual death be just as serene.
MID_LGA_1_M11_Nin_m01: <BLN>So...sleepy...
MID_LGV_1_M11_Bon_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_Bon_m01_001: It may be more widely known than I would like,\nbut our kingdom is facing a small crisis.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Bon_m01_002: Queen Theodora has returned home to deal with it.\nNow, ordinarily I would be at her side.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Bon_m01_003: But Her Majesty has Tobias to look after her, so all\nwill be well.
MID_LGA_1_M11_Bon_m01: <BLN>Has everyone already heard?
MID_LGV_1_M11_Tob_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_Tob_m01_001: There's been some trouble in Saramis, so the boss\nwent back home with Bona.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Tob_m01_002: The two of them are probably mopping the floor with\nthose southern bastards as we speak.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Tob_m01_003: Baw haw haw! I'm not worried about 'em. The boss\nand Bona are an unbeatable pair.
MID_LGA_1_M11_Tob_m01: <BLN>The boss is taking care of business.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Lil_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_Lil_m01_001: I worry about my father...he can be kinda pathetic.\nFortunately, my mother is a lot more put-together.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Lil_m01_002: I doubt she'd let him get swept up in the coup.\nAnd they'd never side with the Mosa.
MID_LGA_1_M11_Lil_m01: <BLN>I worry about him sometimes.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Lys_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_Lys_m01_001: Saramis is going through a crisis. Would that I could\nbe there to help!
MID_LGV_1_M11_Lys_m01_002: But I must focus on what I can contribute here.\nThose were Her Majesty's orders.
MID_LGA_1_M11_Lys_m01: <BLN>Saramis is in crisis.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Buc_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_Buc_m01_001: She may try to hide it, but I can tell milady is\ngrowing more and more worn down by the day.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Buc_m01_002: I fear Obsidian truly is... Well. In any case, hopefully\nall ends well.
MID_LGA_1_M11_Buc_m01: <BLN>Milady's condition...
MID_LGV_1_M11_Sci_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_Sci_m01_001: Aha! It's humbling how many men hate me for my\ngood looks. "He's as bad as Dietrich," I hear them say.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Sci_m01_002: As if I could be one moment calm—and the next\nlashing out with murderous intent, sharp as a gale!
MID_LGV_1_M11_Sci_m01_003: Still, all great men are clad in the wind.
MID_LGA_1_M11_Sci_m01: <BLN>It's humbling.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Moo_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_Moo_m01_001: The other day I saw a mom and her kid walking\ndown the street, chatting and laughing.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Moo_m01_002: It seemed like they really got along...like they were\njust friends with an age gap.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Moo_m01_003: It kinda made me jealous.
MID_LGA_1_M11_Moo_m01: <BLN>They seemed so happy.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Mic_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_Mic_m01_001: Ugh... Now this is a pain.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Mic_m01_002: People keep wanting to spar with me, because I'm\nMikaela Redblade.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Mic_m01_003: I tell them I'm not really a mercenary anymore, but\nthey won't take no for an answer.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Mic_m01_004: <NCA>Speak of her renown.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Mic_m01_005: <NCB>Suggest she refuse.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Mic_m01_006: <ACA>You know, now that you mention it, it's not so bad\nto be famous, is it? I guess I shouldn't shy from it.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Mic_m01_007: <ACB>But it'd be bad to turn down someone who went out\nof their way to find me, wouldn't it?
MID_LGA_1_M11_Mic_m01: <BLN>They keep finding me!
MID_LGV_1_M11_Oly_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_Oly_m01_001: For any artist, it is a great honor to be named the\nRose of Caelus at the Rose Pageant.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Oly_m01_002: I won the contest the year after losing to Leilidahna,\nthough I was not selected.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Oly_m01_003: Not until my second victory was I chosen. Which is\nto say some things cannot be gained by winning.
MID_LGA_1_M11_Oly_m01: <BLN>The Rose of Caelus.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Naz_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_Naz_m01_001: Some guy called Sha Lan a "worrywart." And then,\njust when I started to wonder what they'd call me...
MID_LGV_1_M11_Naz_m01_002: they called me "Mr. Hothead," and that kinda felt\nlike they were making fun of me!
MID_LGA_1_M11_Naz_m01: <BLN>Is that what I'm like?
MID_LGV_1_M11_Sar_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_Sar_m01_001: There's plenty of food and water here. No wonder\nthe people who live near Dagsion are so happy.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Sar_m01_002: They can't even imagine suffering hunger, or what it\nwould be like to lose their home.
MID_LGA_1_M11_Sar_m01: <BLN>They can't imagine.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Dai_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_Dai_m01_001: Anatolia is an amazing woman and I know she'll be\nfine, no matter what happens.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Dai_m01_002: Nowadays it seems like she's always angry at me.\nBut the first time she looked at me, I was so happy.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Dai_m01_003: And, ya know, nobody else came to see me when I\nwas in solitary confinement. But she did.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Dai_m01_004: Oh no! Please don't tell Anatolia anything I just said!\nI'd die of embarrassment if she knew!
MID_LGA_1_M11_Dai_m01: <BLN>She's such an amazing woman.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Hal_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_Hal_m01_001: Sometimes, when I've been in the city for too long,\nI start to wish I could smell some farm air.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Hal_m01_002: That scent brings to mind the wonderful feeling\nof freshly turned soil.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Hal_m01_003: I mean, the city is nice, but the countryside is\nso much more relaxing.
MID_LGA_1_M11_Hal_m01: <BLN>The city is nice, but...
MID_LGV_1_M11_Guj_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_Guj_m01_001: Long ago, two of the gods had themselves an\nepic battle over me—Jurah and Kalla.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Guj_m01_002: I calmed them as best I could, because their clash\ncould have torn the land of Dagda in two.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Guj_m01_003: And that's why this continent has known peace for\nso long now. But hell, it was a CLOSE call.
MID_LGA_1_M11_Guj_m01: <BLN>I may have sinned, but...
MID_LGV_1_M11_Yan_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_Yan_m01_001: My life of wandering once saw me collapse, but a\npassing farmer saved me from death.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Yan_m01_002: That farmer and I still correspond to this day,\ntrading delicacies and bottles of drink.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Yan_m01_003: In the end, people are there for people. It's those\nrelationships that are the only real ones.
MID_LGA_1_M11_Yan_m01: <BLN>Real connections are golden.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Iio_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_Iio_m01_001: Street performers are great fun, working hard to\nsurprise with trick after trick.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Iio_m01_002: But one recently surprised me in a different way,\nconfronting me for being bored by them.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Iio_m01_003: I had no idea I was wearing such a serious look.\nInwardly, I was nothing but delighted.
MID_LGA_1_M11_Iio_m01: <BLN>My face is just this way.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Pep_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_Pep_m01_001: We believe that one of the groups in the Heroic\nGames crossed over from Brigid to attend.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Pep_m01_002: We can tell without even speaking to them. Their\nbearing when walking and battling says it all.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Pep_m01_003: They are far and away from their homeland but\nstill carry home with them in their bones.
MID_LGA_1_M11_Pep_m01: <BLN>We can tell.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Noc_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_Noc_m01_001: I get the sense that everything is noisy\neverywhere you go here! Such excitement!
MID_LGV_1_M11_Noc_m01_002: I feel the same way, but I have to be careful that I\ndon't get TOO caught up in it.
MID_LGA_1_M11_Noc_m01: <BLN>I get SO excited!
MID_LGV_1_M11_Sop_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_Sop_m01_001: I'm hoping we're finally getting to the point where\nAnna is able to take a break.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Sop_m01_002: Still, it seems harder than ever for her right now.\nI gave her a shoulder rub, and she was so stiff.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Sop_m01_003: When her work with the Heroic Games is over,\nI should treat her to something special!
MID_LGA_1_M11_Sop_m01: <BLN>Now that it's winding down...
MID_LGV_1_M11_Cat_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_Cat_m01_001: Finally! I managed to discover a trader who knows\nthe true and proper value of things.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Cat_m01_002: I've been wanting to sell some items that I no\nlonger need but couldn't find a decent buyer.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Cat_m01_003: If you can't gauge true quality, how can you even\nbuy something for its proper price?
MID_LGA_1_M11_Cat_m01: <BLN>Finally!
MID_LGV_1_M11_Ned_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_Ned_m01_001: Working as a mercenary, I've had many of my\nclients look down on me or think me disposable.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Ned_m01_002: Of course, it's always those people who change\ntheir tune when the battle turns against them.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Ned_m01_003: You can't always trust people. And maybe influential\npeople even less so.
MID_LGA_1_M11_Ned_m01: <BLN>Working as a mercenary...
MID_LGV_1_M11_Zac_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_Zac_m01_001: The Heroic Games are finally shuttin' up shop\nsoon. Crazy I've barely earned squat!
MID_LGV_1_M11_Zac_m01_002: I had my eye on some folks, but those damn\ntemple guards were prowlin' around.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Zac_m01_003: Ugh...that spoils the fun. Wish those guys would\njust curl up and die already.
MID_LGA_1_M11_Zac_m01: <BLN>Miserable!
MID_LGV_1_M11_Maj_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_Maj_m01_001: I'm a pretty huge guy, yeah. But there are huger\nguys in the world.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Maj_m01_002: I don't like that. Nope, not at ALL. They better\nnot have a big attitude around ME.
MID_LGA_1_M11_Maj_m01: <BLN>I don't like it at ALL!
MID_LGV_1_M11_Ven_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_Ven_m01_001: Has every soul here forgotten about my\nexcellence? My sheer brilliance?
MID_LGV_1_M11_Ven_m01_002: What does it matter if I lost in the games? I'm a\ngeneral! I've shared my flashes of genius!
MID_LGV_1_M11_Ven_m01_003: I'll trumpet my greatness if I must! All must\nremember! All must applaud!
MID_LGA_1_M11_Ven_m01: <BLN>They WILL remember me!
MID_LGV_1_M11_Ini_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_Ini_m01_001: I heard about Simon while walking the city, and\nI'm left wondering if he caused some trouble.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Ini_m01_002: I recall that he tends to have trouble around him... \nSomething about women... Hmm...
MID_LGA_1_M11_Ini_m01: <BLN>That Simon...
MID_LGV_1_M11_Jas_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_Jas_m01_001: The guys who beat my mercenary crew put on a\ngood show during the main matches.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Jas_m01_002: That works out nicely for the Rains of Palma.\nIt's an honor that we fought against them.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Jas_m01_003: I bet my crew will get even more job requests now.
MID_LGA_1_M11_Jas_m01: <BLN>All good by me.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Ale_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_Ale_m01_001: Jurah doesn't venture outside very often, and she\nmeets only with the gods she's closest with.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Ale_m01_002: She's entrusted the affairs of her temple to others.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Ale_m01_003: So everyone at her temple understands that they\nmust live up to her silent expectations of them.
MID_LGA_1_M11_Ale_m01: <BLN>About Jurah...
MID_LGV_1_M11_Cen_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_Cen_m01_001: Temple soldiers are trained to be the best. They\nare the strength of the empire and of the temples.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Cen_m01_002: When you see them on patrol, you can feel their\npride in their service.
MID_LGA_1_M11_Cen_m01: <BLN>They're very well trained...
MID_LGV_1_M11_Kir_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_Kir_m01_001: It must be great to be a god. I'd like to be one...\na god of pirates.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Kir_m01_002: Then I could do anything! And...I wouldn't be\nterrified of ghosts anymore.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Kir_m01_003: Most of all, a goddess would have eyes for me,\nand her beauty would be mine, all mine!
MID_LGA_1_M11_Kir_m01: <BLN>To be a god...
MID_LGV_1_M11_Nuz_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_Nuz_m01_001: Sometimes I worry whether I did the right thing\nas acting chief.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Nuz_m01_002: I suppose it is a form of weakness. Victory rarely\ngoes to those who are indecisive.
MID_LGA_1_M11_Nuz_m01: <BLN>I worry sometimes...
MID_LGV_1_M11_Gab_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_Gab_m01_001: Some folks, they serve out their sentences, go free,\nand get themselves thrown right back in prison.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Gab_m01_002: Though, I do give my prisoners a decent meal...
MID_LGV_1_M11_Gab_m01_003: I'd hate to think they had trouble finding food on the\noutside, and that's why they came back.
MID_LGA_1_M11_Gab_m01: <BLN>It's strange.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Lin_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_Lin_m01_001: Sounded like quite a commotion here last month.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Lin_m01_002: But I welcome anything that distracts me from\nmy situation.
MID_LGA_1_M11_Lin_m01: <BLN>Quite a commotion.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Nat_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_Nat_m01_001: The old royalists have been eradicated in Arago,\nwhile the chancellor's faction gains power.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Nat_m01_002: And the sad irony is that Queen Aswan, who has\nKing Hasdrubal's blood, is kept away from politics.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Nat_m01_003: But my allegiance is to whoever sits on the throne.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Nat_m01_004: For as long as that's King Gilchris, it is to him I\npledge my loyalty.
MID_LGA_1_M11_Nat_m01: <BLN>The situation in Arago.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Hri_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_Hri_m01_001: With the Heroic Games coming to a close, our king\nand queen will likely return to Arago.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Hri_m01_002: And during the journey, we will probably accompany\nthem as guards.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Hri_m01_003: I only hope the king doesn't throw one of his\ntantrums while we're on the road.
MID_LGA_1_M11_Hri_m01: <BLN>After the games end...
MID_LGV_1_M11_Ann_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_Ann_m01_001: I'm going to give my business everything I've got this\nmonth! I've stocked up on a lot of great stuff.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Ann_m01_002: Are you sure you're fully prepared for what's to\ncome? If you forgot anything, you can get it from me!
MID_LGA_1_M11_Ann_m01: <BLN>Are you fully prepared?
MID_LGV_1_M11_Cle_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_Cle_m01_001: Take a look at these hovels, and the buckets these\ninsects call boats!
MID_LGV_1_M11_Cle_m01_002: There's no way these things are seaworthy! We are\ncapital-F...fish out of water.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Cle_m01_003: Ah, well. At least the humidity is good for my skin.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Cle_m01_004: But the sea breeze is just flinging salt at me, so we'll\ncall it a wash.
MID_LGA_1_M11_Cle_m01: <BLN>Salty!
MID_LGV_1_M11_Mys_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_Mys_m01_001: There are several ports to the north, but few seem to\nbe open to travelers.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Mys_m01_002: Taking everything into consideration, I'd recommend\nwe head west, to Niiza Port.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Mys_m01_003: There are some villages along the way too. For\nstarters, we'll head to Kassite.
MID_LGV_1_M11_Mys_m01_004: Should be an easy trip. Unless that damned\nCleobulus finds a way to muck it up.
MID_LGA_1_M11_Mys_m01: <BLN>Should be an easy trip. 
MID_LGV_1_M11_B01_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_B01_m01_001: Lately I seem to be burning a lot of dishes in the\ndining hall. I just keep spacing out...
MID_LGV_1_M11_B01_m01_002: My boss says it's because I have a crush, but is that\nreally it? Nah...it can't be...
MID_LGV_1_M11_B01_m01_003: Sure, Queen Theodora is beautiful and dignified, but\nfalling for a Saraminian? And a queen, at that?
MID_LGV_1_M11_B01_m01_004: Wait—YOU'RE Queen Theodora! What are you\ndoing in my humble dining hall?!
MID_LGA_1_M11_B01_m01: <BLN>Nah, it can't be...
MID_LGV_1_M11_B02_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_B02_m01_001: An awful lot of people drop half-empty ghosh bottles\nand used skewers around before heading home.
MID_LGV_1_M11_B02_m01_002: The Heroic Games are supposed to be sacred!\nWhy do they seem to bring out the worst in people?
MID_LGV_1_M11_B02_m01_003: First thing tomorrow, the cleanup will begin. I dread\nto think how much of it will fall to the priests.
MID_LGA_1_M11_B02_m01: <BLN>How revolting...
MID_LGV_1_M11_B03_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_B03_m01_001: Staring out at the arena, I think back to those intense\nmatches. I want to remember every detail.
MID_LGV_1_M11_B03_m01_002: I may never see greater battles as long as I live.\nI'm glad I found the time to watch them.
MID_LGA_1_M11_B03_m01: <BLN>I'm glad I came!
MID_LGV_1_M11_B04_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_B04_m01_001: My son fought in the games as a gladiator. I couldn't\nhelp but fret over him getting horribly injured.
MID_LGV_1_M11_B04_m01_002: Things can be repaired or replaced, but family...
MID_LGA_1_M11_B04_m01: <BLN>I couldn't help but worry.
MID_LGV_1_M11_B05_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_B05_m01_001: Songs about the White-Maned Demon go over well\nwith everyone—women and men, young and old.
MID_LGV_1_M11_B05_m01_002: But you can only sing about the same subject for so\nlong. Hope a new warrior arises for fresh material.
MID_LGA_1_M11_B05_m01: <BLN>Sure, they love him now...
MID_LGV_1_M11_B06_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_B06_m01_001: That husband of mine forgot something again! I don't\ncare how busy priests are—this is ridiculous!
MID_LGV_1_M11_B06_m01_002: Whenever I bring it up, he just says it's because he\nhas his hands full taking care of Smyrnos.
MID_LGV_1_M11_B06_m01_003: Has he no shame, blaming his own shortcomings\non the gods?!
MID_LGA_1_M11_B06_m01: <BLN>That husband of mine!
MID_LGV_1_M11_B07_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_B07_m01_001: I'd better offer some prayers at Mars's temple before\nI make the trip home, just for safety.
MID_LGV_1_M11_B07_m01_002: With the Bringer of War's blessing, if any bandits\nattack me on the way, I'll send 'em flying!
MID_LGA_1_M11_B07_m01: <BLN>With Mars's blessing...
MID_LGV_1_M11_B08_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_B08_m01_001: That damned temple soldier! He drove me off,\nsaying I was just a common beggar!
MID_LGV_1_M11_B08_m01_002: I'd only come to pray. Maybe I should jump him\nwhen he's alone after his shift...
MID_LGA_1_M11_B08_m01: <BLN>Just you wait!
MID_LGV_1_M11_B09_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_B09_m01_001: I supply Mars's temple with blades. But no matter\nhow many I make, I'm not confident in their quality.
MID_LGV_1_M11_B09_m01_002: Unless it's something so extraordinary that everyone\nin Dagda takes notice, it'll never be worthy of him.
MID_LGA_1_M11_B09_m01: <BLN>This isn't up to scratch...
MID_LGV_1_M11_B10_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_B10_m01_001: Most mercenaries who entered the Heroic Games\nfound employers as a result.
MID_LGV_1_M11_B10_m01_002: I made a mistake not entering because I thought I\ncouldn't possibly win. Maybe I should say I did enter.
MID_LGA_1_M11_B10_m01: <BLN>What a blunder...
MID_LGV_1_M11_B11_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_B11_m01_001: My mom's always saying it's "time for you to\ngrow up!" Especially when she's had a few.
MID_LGV_1_M11_B11_m01_002: She's been a mess ever since Dad died in the arena.
MID_LGA_1_M11_B11_m01: <BLN>My mom's on my case...
MID_LGV_1_M11_B12_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_B12_m01_001: I'm looking after a kid whose parents disappeared.\nThey came here from another county to find work.
MID_LGV_1_M11_B12_m01_002: But I guess they couldn't find a decent job, so they\nleft the kid behind to ease the burden.
MID_LGV_1_M11_B12_m01_003: I dunno if I can afford to raise a kid either, but I can't\njust look the other way.
MID_LGA_1_M11_B12_m01: <BLN>Call it fate, I guess.
MID_LGV_1_M11_B13_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_B13_m01_001: My grandpa is a master angler. He knows everything\nabout every kind of fish.
MID_LGV_1_M11_B13_m01_002: Not that it matters, since all he does is deep-fry\nwhatever he catches.
MID_LGA_1_M11_B13_m01: <BLN>Fish is delicious, isn't it?
MID_LGV_1_M11_B14_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_B14_m01_001: Stables have a very distinctive smell, don't they?\nSome people really don't care for it.
MID_LGV_1_M11_B14_m01_002: In my younger days, I took special care to keep\nclean, but over the years it became a real hassle.
MID_LGV_1_M11_B14_m01_003: Do this for long enough, and it soaks into your skin,\nbecoming part of you.
MID_LGA_1_M11_B14_m01: <BLN>The stables are a part of me now.
MID_LGV_1_M11_B15_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_B15_m01_001: My dad's been going on and on at home about the\nprophet Jehoshaphat.
MID_LGV_1_M11_B15_m01_002: Always saying that when the world's in turmoil,\nthe Herald will show up, and all that.
MID_LGV_1_M11_B15_m01_003: So isn't it actually better if it doesn't happen? I mean,\nif the world is at peace, no need for the Herald.
MID_LGA_1_M11_B15_m01: <BLN>I'm sick of hearing it.
MID_LGV_1_M11_B16_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_B16_m01_001: Young folks always want to get into the thermae as\nsoon as they get a chill from the breeze off the water.
MID_LGV_1_M11_B16_m01_002: But then they get so hot that they're drenched in\nsweat. They should do what I do—swim in the river!
MID_LGA_1_M11_B16_m01: <BLN>What's so special about it?
MID_LGV_1_M11_B17_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_B17_m01_001: My boyfriend has been so busy with his priest work\nthat we haven't gotten together for a whole year.
MID_LGV_1_M11_B17_m01_002: But he said that once cleanup for the Heroic Games\nis done, he'll take a long holiday. That'll be nice.
MID_LGV_1_M11_B17_m01_003: I don't care if we spend it traveling or relaxing at\nhome—as long as we're together, I'm happy.
MID_LGA_1_M11_B17_m01: <BLN>I can't wait!
MID_LGV_1_M11_B18_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_B18_m01_001: The folks from Saramis sure left in a hurry.
MID_LGV_1_M11_B18_m01_002: They were loud when they arrived, and now they're\nloud when they leave. What a bunch of savages.
MID_LGA_1_M11_B18_m01: <BLN>Those brutes from Saramis...
MID_LGV_1_M11_B19_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_B19_m01_001: I can scarcely believe the house I visited had that\ntricolor vase from the east. And it was so pristine!
MID_LGV_1_M11_B19_m01_002: It's a miracle that it made it safely across the sea for\nme to discover here in the capital.
MID_LGV_1_M11_B19_m01_003: The flow of the glaze was perfect upon the flawless\ncast... Just remembering it gets me excited all over.
MID_LGA_1_M11_B19_m01: <BLN>I can scarcely believe it!
MID_LGV_1_M11_B20_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_B20_m01_001: Now that the case is solved, I thought that Aurora\nmight show herself.
MID_LGV_1_M11_B20_m01_002: But nothing's changed yet. What must the Divine\nSovereign think of his daughter?
MID_LGA_1_M11_B20_m01: <BLN>Since the case was resolved...
MID_LGV_1_M11_B21_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_B21_m01_001: No sailor worth his salt will go near the Isle of Balor\nin Cybele.
MID_LGV_1_M11_B21_m01_002: I can't say too much else, but know that it's a very\ndangerous place to visit.
MID_LGA_1_M11_B21_m01: <BLN>Don't risk your life.
MID_LGV_1_M11_B22_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_B22_m01_001: A while ago, I tried to buy one of Drake's treasures\nfor myself.
MID_LGV_1_M11_B22_m01_002: Turns out, it was a fake. I waited and waited,\nbut nothing special happened.
MID_LGV_1_M11_B22_m01_003: I was so angry that I caught the guy who sold it to\nme and dumped him in Lake Baal.
MID_LGA_1_M11_B22_m01: <BLN>I just want a look at the real thing...
MID_LGV_1_M11_B23_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M11_B23_m01_001: Don't you ever get tired of showing up here month in,\nmonth out?
MID_LGV_1_M11_B23_m01_003: There's nothing past this door that concerns you.\nGet it? So don't come back.
MID_LGV_1_M11_B23_m01_002: If you're trying to wear me down, it won't work.\nYou're not gettin' in there.
MID_LGA_1_M11_B23_m01: <BLN>This isn't getting you anywhere.